Building this package
=====================

Two artifacts must be staged into the source tree before building, because
neither is in the upstream release tarball and the build has no network:

1. resources/xfce-wayland-protocols/
   A git submodule of custom XFCE Wayland protocol XML. Unpack
   https://gitlab.xfce.org/xfce/xfce-wayland-protocols/-/archive/<rev>/...tar.gz
   there with --strip-components=1. src/protocols/*.rs reference it by
   relative path via wayland_scanner::generate_*!, so the path is exact.

2. vendor/
   Cargo.toml pulls smithay from git, which cargo cannot fetch offline.
   Produce with `cargo vendor` against the pinned Cargo.lock. debian/rules
   installs debian/cargo-config.toml as .cargo/config.toml to redirect both
   crates.io and the smithay git source at it.

An upstream patch is also required (see debian/patches): the cfg gate on
WlrBufferConstraints.dma omits the udev feature while three call sites guard
it under udev, so a udev-only build does not compile without it. This needs
debian/source/format to be "3.0 (quilt)" or dpkg-source silently never
applies it — confirmed by building without that file present: no error, no
warning, the patch is simply not there and the build fails at the dma field
instead, which looks like a different bug entirely.


Debian trixie (rustc 1.85) cannot build this commit — verified, not assumed
=============================================================================

Built end to end on trixie against real trixie repos (not vendored — cargo
was allowed to fetch, to isolate the actual blocker). Two independent
version floors, both confirmed by building rather than inferred from specs:

1. `image` is a DIRECT dependency pinned `^0.25.1`. The pinned Cargo.lock
   resolves 0.25.10, whose MSRV is rustc 1.88; trixie ships 1.85. Fixed by
   `cargo update -p image --precise 0.25.1`, which still satisfies the
   `^0.25.1` constraint and has a lower MSRV. Confirmed 0.25.1 through
   0.25.6 all resolve; 0.25.1 was used.

   This means trixie needs its OWN vendor tarball, not the RPM/Fedora one —
   Fedora's rustc (1.96) has no trouble with 0.25.10, and re-vendoring here
   would downgrade it for no reason on that base.

2. Past that, xfwl4's OWN code fails: src/core/input_handler.rs calls
   `argv0.display()` on an OsStr, using `OsStr::display()`, a library
   feature not yet stabilized on rustc 1.85 (error: "use of unstable
   library feature os_str_display"). This is not a dependency version
   problem — it is xfwl4's pinned commit requiring a newer rustc than
   trixie ships, full stop. No packaging change fixes it; either xfwl4
   gains a rustc-1.85-compatible formatting call upstream, or trixie needs
   a newer rustc than its own repos provide.

So flounder (Debian trixie) is blocked on this commit's own MSRV, not on
anything in this packaging.

Debian sid / Ubuntu — evidenced, not yet build-verified
=========================================================
sid ships rustc 1.95.0, Ubuntu resolute ships 1.93.1 (both measured
directly) — comfortably past both floors above. flounder-sid and grouper
should build against the STANDARD vendor tree (same one the RPM spec uses,
image=0.25.10 and all), with no need for the trixie-specific downgrade.
This is a strong expectation from the version numbers, not a build that has
actually been run — do not read it as verified until someone builds it.
